[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/383502626","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/4616#issuecomment-383502626","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/4616","id":383502626,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4MzUwMjYyNg==","user":{"login":"andrewbaxter","id":597549,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NzU0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/597549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter","html_url":"https://github.com/andrewbaxter","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andrewbaxter/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-04-23T08:52:52Z","updated_at":"2018-04-23T08:52:52Z","body":"Is this the same as:\r\n\r\n```\r\nclass A:\r\n    x = 4\r\n\r\n\r\ni: type = A\r\nassert issubclass(i, A)\r\nprint(i.x)\r\n```\r\nwhich fails with:\r\n```\r\n7: error: \"type\" has no attribute \"x\"\r\n```\r\n?\r\n\r\nmypy 0.590\r\n\r\nIt looks like `issubclass` doesn't imply anything AFAICT, unlike `isinstance`.\r\n\r\nThere's this workaround:\r\n```\r\ni: type = A\r\nj: Type[A] = i\r\nprint(j.x)\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut since this isn't in assertion format it seems more like a static check omission.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/383502626/reactions","total_count":0,"+1