.github.com/repos/python/mypy/deployments","created_at":"2012-12-07T13:30:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T11:48:01Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-11T20:11:30Z","git_url":"git://github.com/python/mypy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:python/mypy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy","homepage":"https://www.mypy-lang.org/","size":77161,"stargazers_count":20064,"watchers_count":20064,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":3065,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"When running mypy on the following code:\r\n```py\r\nclass C:\r\n    @classmethod\r\n    def cm(cls):\r\n        return 1\r\n\r\ndef f(t: type) -> int:\r\n    if issubclass(t, C):\r\n        reveal_type(t)\r\n        return t.cm()\r\n    return 0\r\n```\r\nIt reports:\r\n```\r\n8: error: Revealed type is 'builtins.type'\r\n9: error: \"type\" has no attribute \"cm\"\r\n```\r\nSo in the `if` body, mypy considers the type of `t` to be `type`, while the fact that `issubclass` returned `True` indicates that `t` is of type `C`.\r\n\r\nUsing `issubclass` in this way is the topic of #2909, but that issue was fixed, so there is probably something different in my use case that isn't covered by the existing unit tests.\r\n\r\nI'm using a mypy 0.660 dev snapshot.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/6099/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0